  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🎮 Kids' Gamertag Generator",
      "tagline": "Fun, safe usernames for gaming, with nothing that gives you away."
    },
    "intro": "A good gamertag for a child is fun to say and gives nothing away: no real name, no age, no school. The **Kids' Gamertag Generator** makes safe gaming usernames for children, cool, funny, cute or epic, with no real names, ages, game or brand names, and nothing rude.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good gamertags for kids",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>ArcticRaven</strong>: cool and quick to type.</li><li><strong>NeonDash</strong>: short, fast-sounding and easy to read on a scoreboard.</li><li><strong>CaptainTeapot123</strong>: funny, with a number that isn't an age or a year.</li><li><strong>ProfessorNugget3000</strong>: silly enough to make friends laugh.</li><li><strong>FluffyOtter</strong>: cute and friendly.</li><li><strong>Twinkle_Koala</strong>: cute, with an underscore to keep the words apart.</li><li><strong>TitanKing</strong>: epic, for a player who likes to win.</li><li><strong>PickleTeacup</strong>: two random words that are hard to forget.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "A quick online-safety tip",
        "content": "<p>A good gamertag tells other players nothing about you. Before you choose one, check it doesn't include:</p><ul><li><strong>your real name</strong>, or your surname;</li><li><strong>your age or birthday</strong>, so no 11, 2015 or similar;</li><li><strong>your school, town or street</strong>;</li><li>anything you wouldn't want a stranger to know.</li></ul><p>Every name here follows those rules, and the numbers it adds are never ages or years. Grown-ups: it's worth choosing the name together and checking the game's privacy settings while you're there.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Styles and formats",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Cool</strong> names pair speed and nature: <em>NeonDash</em>, <em>ArcticRaven</em>.</li><li><strong>Funny</strong> names give a food or an animal a grand title: <em>CaptainTeapot</em>, <em>DoctorMuffin</em>.</li><li><strong>Cute</strong> names are soft animals and sweet things: <em>Honey_Squirrel</em>, <em>Daisy_Lamb</em>.</li><li><strong>Epic</strong> names sound like a champion: <em>TitanKing</em>.</li></ul><p>If a name is taken, choose <strong>With a number</strong> or <strong>With an underscore</strong> for a version that's more likely to be free. The numbers are never ages or years.</p><p>Playing Minecraft? Try the <a href=\"minecraft-username-generator.html\">Minecraft Username Generator</a>, which keeps to Minecraft's 16-character limit. For older players, the <a href=\"gamertag-generator.html\">Gamertag Generator</a> has more styles.</p><p>For more characters, see all the <a href=\"../categories/people-names.html\">character name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is a good gamertag for a kid?",
        "answer": "Something fun that doesn't give away personal details, like ArcticRaven, FluffyOtter or CaptainTeapot123. Avoid real names, ages, birthdays, schools and towns."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should a child's gamertag have their age in it?",
        "answer": "No. A number like 11 or 2015 tells strangers how old they are. The numbers this generator adds are never ages or years."
      },
      {
        "question": "What if the gamertag is already taken?",
